1
00:00:01,584 --> 00:00:02,877
<i>Your relationship with Caloy?</i>

2
00:00:02,961 --> 00:00:04,796
<i>- We don't have a relationship.</i>
- [JORDAN] <i>You don't?</i>

3
00:00:04,879 --> 00:00:06,172
<i>- That's nonsense.</i>
<i>- Really?</i>

4
00:00:07,507 --> 00:00:10,093
[BEA] <i>Do you know I'm getting</i>
<i>in trouble because of you?</i>

5
00:00:10,176 --> 00:00:11,803
<i>Just leave me alone.</i>

6
00:00:11,886 --> 00:00:15,181
<i>Because they think we're accomplices.</i>

7
00:00:16,182 --> 00:00:18,018
<i>I could even go to jail because of you.</i>

8
00:00:18,101 --> 00:00:20,145
<i>So please, I'm begging you.</i>

9
00:00:20,228 --> 00:00:23,231
<i>Please, please. Stay away from me.</i>

10
00:00:23,857 --> 00:00:25,692
[BILLY] <i>What are you doing here?</i>

11
00:00:25,775 --> 00:00:27,402
<i>Can you please talk to your people?</i>

12
00:00:27,485 --> 00:00:29,112
<i>Let the world know that I'm a criminal?!</i>

13
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:31,364
<i>Do you think you're going to scare me?</i>

14
00:00:31,448 --> 00:00:33,700
<i>Enjoy your freedom</i>
<i>because it won't last long.</i>

15
00:00:33,783 --> 00:00:34,951
<i>And by the way,</i>

16
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:37,495
<i>orange looks good on you.</i>

17
00:00:40,665 --> 00:00:42,208
<i>Wow!</i>

18
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:44,252
<i>You're up early, Ms. Supervisor.</i>

19
00:00:44,335 --> 00:00:47,672
<i>I have a lot of work to do as supervisor.</i>

20
00:00:47,756 --> 00:00:50,008
<i>- Hmm? Do your best, dear.</i>
- [CHUCKLES]

21
00:00:50,091 --> 00:00:52,218
<i>I will, like I always do.</i>

22
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:54,179
<i>All right, take care!</i>

23
00:01:00,602 --> 00:01:04,272
[WOMAN 1] <i>Sorry, Ms. Mercado,</i>
<i>but we can't process your application</i>

24
00:01:04,355 --> 00:01:05,982
<i>without a police clearance.</i>

25
00:01:06,066 --> 00:01:08,526
[WOMAN 2] <i>Miss, you have a pending case?</i>

26
00:01:08,610 --> 00:01:11,780
[WOMAN 3] <i>We can't hire you, Ms. Mercado.</i>

27
00:01:11,863 --> 00:01:15,867
<i>Your involvement with Carlos Toledo</i>
<i>is all over social media.</i>

28
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:19,704
<i>We don't accept applicants</i>
<i>with connections or ties to criminals.</i>

29
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:21,623
[PHONE RINGING]

30
00:01:21,706 --> 00:01:24,667
<i>Pres. Do you have any plans later?</i>

31
00:01:24,751 --> 00:01:25,794
[PRECIOUS] <i>Why?</i>

32
00:01:27,295 --> 00:01:29,297
<i>There's something I want to tell you.</i>

33
00:01:30,465 --> 00:01:32,509
<i>Hmm… Okay. Sure.</i>

34
00:01:33,802 --> 00:01:35,345
[PRECIOUS SQUEALING]<i> Lydia!</i>

35
00:01:35,428 --> 00:01:37,680
<i>I think he's planning to confess to me!</i>

36
00:01:38,973 --> 00:01:40,016
<i>Yeah.</i>

37
00:01:40,099 --> 00:01:42,310
<i>I didn't expect things would go this fast</i>

38
00:01:42,393 --> 00:01:44,938
<i>after knowing each other</i>
<i>for only a few weeks.</i>

39
00:01:45,021 --> 00:01:47,315
<i>I'm done second-guessing!</i>

40
00:01:47,398 --> 00:01:48,900
<i>I'm taking the risk!</i>

41
00:01:48,983 --> 00:01:51,236
[LUCY] <i>That's the right decision, Enrico.</i>

42
00:01:51,319 --> 00:01:55,240
<i>You need to tell your children's</i>
<i>mother figure the truth about who you are.</i>

43
00:01:55,990 --> 00:01:57,700
<i>Even if there's a chance</i>

44
00:01:58,618 --> 00:02:00,495
<i>she'll get angry with me</i>

45
00:02:00,578 --> 00:02:02,747
<i>and I won't get to see my children again?</i>

46
00:02:03,456 --> 00:02:06,751
<i>What's important is that you're honest</i>

47
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:09,003
<i>with the person who loves them.</i>

48
00:02:09,671 --> 00:02:11,422
<i>And with the woman you love.</i>

49
00:02:12,215 --> 00:02:14,217
<i>You love Precious, don't you?</i>

50
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:18,638
<i>Looks like you've had quite a few.</i>

51
00:02:18,721 --> 00:02:19,764
<i>Not really.</i>

52
00:02:19,848 --> 00:02:21,724
<i>Have you ordered? What do you want?</i>

53
00:02:21,808 --> 00:02:23,601
<i>Oh, nothing. I'm fine.</i>

54
00:02:23,685 --> 00:02:25,270
<i>I'll just have whatever you're having.</i>

55
00:02:25,353 --> 00:02:28,857
<i>Precious, there's something</i>
<i>I need to confess.</i>

56
00:02:31,317 --> 00:02:32,652
[HESITATES]

57
00:02:32,735 --> 00:02:34,195
<i>I'm torn.</i>

58
00:02:34,279 --> 00:02:36,281
<i>I don't know if I should tell you.</i>

59
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:38,616
<i>I'm afraid you'll get angry.</i>

60
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:41,953
<i>I won't get angry.</i>
<i>What is it you want to tell me?</i>

61
00:02:43,121 --> 00:02:44,414
[VOICE BREAKING] <i>Precious…</i>

62
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:48,334
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

63
00:02:51,254 --> 00:02:53,423
<i>But the truth is…</i>

64
00:02:53,506 --> 00:02:55,091
<i>I love you too.</i>

65
00:02:58,887 --> 00:03:00,889
<i>Are we good? Okay?</i>

66
00:03:02,724 --> 00:03:03,975
<i>Okay.</i>

67
00:03:16,863 --> 00:03:19,866
Contact party giveaway supplier.

68
00:03:19,949 --> 00:03:24,579
Confirm orders of flowers
for the centerpiece, okay.

69
00:03:25,204 --> 00:03:26,915
Centerpiece, okay.

70
00:03:26,998 --> 00:03:29,250
Follow up catering

71
00:03:29,334 --> 00:03:32,086
and cake supplier.

72
00:03:32,837 --> 00:03:34,422
Hmm. What should we use?

73
00:03:34,505 --> 00:03:37,258
The function room or the main dining room?

74
00:03:39,510 --> 00:03:41,137
We should do it in the function room.

75
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:42,263
It's more private there.

76
00:03:43,681 --> 00:03:44,682
Okay.

77
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:47,268
And let's finalize the menu.
It's going to be tomorrow.

78
00:03:49,479 --> 00:03:52,482
Wait, wait. I want you to
listen to this. Wait.

79
00:03:53,483 --> 00:03:56,027
I think this suits Auntie Pres.

80
00:03:56,110 --> 00:04:02,742
["ABELYANA" BY MAKI PLAYING]

81
00:04:16,881 --> 00:04:18,383
- It's perfect.
- Mm.

82
00:04:18,466 --> 00:04:19,550
- I'm good with that.
- Right?

83
00:04:19,634 --> 00:04:20,593
[MUSIC STOPS]

84
00:04:21,344 --> 00:04:22,595
Nice, right?

85
00:04:22,679 --> 00:04:24,806
- It's great. Perfect.
- Mm-hmm.

86
00:04:24,889 --> 00:04:26,349
You know what, dude?

87
00:04:27,684 --> 00:04:31,271
I didn't think Auntie Pres
would fall in love again

88
00:04:31,938 --> 00:04:36,693
after Uncle Rico died
right on their wedding day.

89
00:04:37,443 --> 00:04:43,074
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

90
00:04:43,157 --> 00:04:45,493
[BILLY] <i>Even after</i>
<i>everything she went through,</i>

91
00:04:45,576 --> 00:04:47,370
<i>she's always smiling.</i>

92
00:04:48,079 --> 00:04:50,999
<i>She's so strong,</i>
<i>you'd never guess what she's been through.</i>

93
00:04:52,208 --> 00:04:59,173
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

94
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:08,683
<i>But ever since someone</i>
<i>opened her heart again,</i>

95
00:05:08,766 --> 00:05:11,144
<i>Auntie Pres has become happier.</i>

96
00:05:11,227 --> 00:05:12,687
<i>Her smiles are just different.</i>

97
00:05:12,770 --> 00:05:18,192
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

98
00:05:18,276 --> 00:05:21,362
<i>She's happy and complete on her own.</i>

99
00:05:21,446 --> 00:05:24,532
<i>But now, she has more reasons to smile.</i>

100
00:05:26,242 --> 00:05:27,785
[NO AUDIBLE DIALOG]

101
00:05:30,371 --> 00:05:34,959
<i>Even if it's uncertain,</i>
<i>many still take risks on love.</i>

102
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:38,880
<i>Because once it happens,</i>

103
00:05:39,756 --> 00:05:41,549
<i>it'll completely change a person's life.</i>

104
00:05:42,508 --> 00:05:49,348
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

105
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:52,477
It's a different sense of happiness
when someone loves you.

106
00:05:55,646 --> 00:05:57,523
And when you love someone too.

107
00:06:00,109 --> 00:06:05,948
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

108
00:06:06,032 --> 00:06:07,075
What?

109
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:09,660
Nothing.

110
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:13,748
Is there anyone we forgot to invite?

111
00:06:13,831 --> 00:06:14,665
Hmm…

112
00:06:14,749 --> 00:06:16,876
You might… have someone in mind?

113
00:06:18,127 --> 00:06:19,253
There is one person.

114
00:06:19,337 --> 00:06:22,507
The man who's making Auntie Pres happy.

115
00:06:24,217 --> 00:06:25,384
Should we invite him?

116
00:06:25,468 --> 00:06:26,636
- Sure!
- Mm-hmm.

117
00:06:27,261 --> 00:06:28,930
All right, I'll ask for his number.

118
00:06:29,013 --> 00:06:35,937
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

119
00:06:39,357 --> 00:06:46,072
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

120
00:07:29,866 --> 00:07:35,997
["ABELYANA" BY MAKI PLAYING]

121
00:07:41,711 --> 00:07:42,879
Dude!

122
00:07:42,962 --> 00:07:44,881
What are you doing?!

123
00:07:47,216 --> 00:07:48,342
This can't be.

124
00:07:48,426 --> 00:07:49,719
[GRUNTS]

125
00:07:51,637 --> 00:07:52,805
[SIGHS]

126
00:07:52,889 --> 00:07:59,770
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

127
00:07:59,854 --> 00:08:03,483
[PLASTIC WRAPPER RUSTLING]

128
00:08:06,611 --> 00:08:09,530
[PLASTIC WRAPPER RUSTLING]

129
00:08:19,373 --> 00:08:21,083
I GOT LOST AGAIN
LIKE I LEARNED NOTHING BEFORE

130
00:08:21,167 --> 00:08:22,793
THOUSANDS OF MILES
I'LL WALK BEFORE GIVING UP

131
00:08:24,003 --> 00:08:31,010
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

132
00:08:31,594 --> 00:08:34,472
JUST TO FIND YOU
AND FOR YOU TO FIND ME TOO

133
00:08:43,397 --> 00:08:45,399
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

134
00:08:52,031 --> 00:08:54,408
Happy birthday to me.

135
00:09:06,796 --> 00:09:08,548
BILLY: SORRY, AUNTIE PRES.

136
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:12,677
THERE'S AN EMERGENCY AT THE OFFICE.

137
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:15,388
I MIGHT GET HOME LATE.

138
00:09:15,471 --> 00:09:16,722
That's it?

139
00:09:17,473 --> 00:09:18,975
No birthday greetings?

140
00:09:20,476 --> 00:09:27,400
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

141
00:09:29,193 --> 00:09:30,611
[PRECIOUS] <i>It's a bit sad.</i>

142
00:09:30,695 --> 00:09:33,406
<i>I don't think anyone</i>
<i>remembered my birthday.</i>

143
00:09:34,115 --> 00:09:36,200
I did! I remembered it's today!

144
00:09:36,784 --> 00:09:38,786
Can I take you out to dinner later?

145
00:09:41,998 --> 00:09:43,040
You can.

146
00:09:43,124 --> 00:09:47,295
Billy's working, and Oliver's camping.

147
00:09:47,378 --> 00:09:49,672
And no one else invited me to anything.

148
00:09:49,755 --> 00:09:51,882
[ENRICO] <i>Isn't that better?</i>
<i>It'd be just the two of us.</i>

149
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:54,218
Okay, sure.

150
00:09:54,302 --> 00:09:57,221
But is it okay if we go to church first?

151
00:09:57,305 --> 00:09:59,640
Yeah, we can meet there.

152
00:09:59,724 --> 00:10:01,392
Is 5:00 p.m. okay with you?

153
00:10:01,475 --> 00:10:03,394
Mm-hmm. [SOFT LAUGH]

154
00:10:05,855 --> 00:10:06,814
Bye.

155
00:10:10,651 --> 00:10:12,820
[MUSIC FADING]

156
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:16,490
- [MAN] Coach Brandon? You have a call.
- [PHONE RINGING]

157
00:10:17,992 --> 00:10:19,160
[BRANDON] Oh, thanks.

158
00:10:21,245 --> 00:10:22,163
Hello?

159
00:10:22,246 --> 00:10:25,666
Hi. Is this Brandon Enriquez?

160
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:27,293
Yeah. Who is this?

161
00:10:27,376 --> 00:10:29,337
Hi, this is Billy.

162
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:31,672
Auntie Precious is my adoptive mother.

163
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:34,050
All right, so is there a problem?

164
00:10:34,133 --> 00:10:36,552
No. No problem at all.

165
00:10:36,636 --> 00:10:37,803
Um…

166
00:10:37,887 --> 00:10:40,222
It's actually her birthday today.

167
00:10:40,931 --> 00:10:42,933
- So what?
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

168
00:10:43,017 --> 00:10:45,853
Um, we're having a surprise party for her,

169
00:10:45,936 --> 00:10:48,189
and we were hoping you could come.

170
00:10:49,065 --> 00:10:50,274
Surprise?

171
00:10:52,151 --> 00:10:53,986
She doesn't know you're inviting me?

172
00:10:54,737 --> 00:10:55,988
No.

173
00:10:56,072 --> 00:10:58,699
Aren't you aware that
we're no longer on good terms?

174
00:10:59,283 --> 00:11:00,451
Um…

175
00:11:00,534 --> 00:11:04,997
She did mention a spat you had, but…

176
00:11:05,539 --> 00:11:07,625
surely you've made amends by now.

177
00:11:07,708 --> 00:11:09,126
Nope.

178
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:11,337
I'll hang up now. I'm busy.

179
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:13,214
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

180
00:11:13,297 --> 00:11:16,008
[HANG-UP TONE]

181
00:11:25,393 --> 00:11:26,477
[MUSIC ENDS]

182
00:11:27,311 --> 00:11:30,481
- I've fallen in love with Precious.
- [MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

183
00:11:30,564 --> 00:11:33,359
I don't want to lose
what we have right now.

184
00:11:35,945 --> 00:11:37,446
But I promise,

185
00:11:38,322 --> 00:11:39,990
at the right time,

186
00:11:41,367 --> 00:11:43,786
I'll tell her everything.

187
00:11:44,954 --> 00:11:48,124
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

188
00:11:48,207 --> 00:11:50,292
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

189
00:12:02,972 --> 00:12:09,937
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

190
00:12:15,568 --> 00:12:16,902
So weird.

191
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:20,739
I really thought Auntie Precious
was going out with Brandon.

192
00:12:22,783 --> 00:12:24,827
Got any idea who the guy is?

193
00:12:25,703 --> 00:12:27,538
She sure knows how to keep a secret.

194
00:12:28,205 --> 00:12:29,623
She didn't tell me a thing!

195
00:12:29,707 --> 00:12:31,917
- [SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]
- Let it go.

196
00:12:35,379 --> 00:12:38,507
Thank you for joining me on my birthday.

197
00:12:38,591 --> 00:12:41,802
Even if it wasn't your birthday,
I'd still want to be with you.

198
00:12:41,886 --> 00:12:43,137
Where do you want to eat?

199
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:45,097
- [PHONE RINGING]
- [STAMMERS]

200
00:12:45,181 --> 00:12:47,349
Excuse me. Oh, I'm sorry.
Give me a second.

201
00:12:48,934 --> 00:12:50,102
Oh.

202
00:12:50,186 --> 00:12:52,646
It's Lydia, my colleague
at Angels of Grace.

203
00:12:52,730 --> 00:12:54,565
She probably just wants to greet me.

204
00:12:54,648 --> 00:12:56,650
Hello? Finally!

205
00:12:56,734 --> 00:12:58,486
Listen, Precious…

206
00:12:58,569 --> 00:13:00,446
Sorry this is so last-minute.

207
00:13:00,529 --> 00:13:03,782
Remember that sponsor
we've been trying to get

208
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:05,743
for Angels of Grace?

209
00:13:05,826 --> 00:13:09,663
Well, he's finally agreed
to meet with us over dinner!

210
00:13:09,747 --> 00:13:10,748
[GASPS]

211
00:13:10,831 --> 00:13:12,416
Oh, thank goodness!

212
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:14,126
I've been praying for this
for a long time!

213
00:13:14,210 --> 00:13:15,711
Okay, okay. When?

214
00:13:15,794 --> 00:13:17,046
Well, here's the thing…

215
00:13:17,129 --> 00:13:19,715
My goodness, it's such short notice.

216
00:13:19,798 --> 00:13:23,552
It's tonight,
7:30 p.m. at the Lasap resto-bar.

217
00:13:24,428 --> 00:13:25,387
What?

218
00:13:25,471 --> 00:13:28,474
That's right. And you'll be
the one doing the talking.

219
00:13:28,557 --> 00:13:31,268
You'll explain the advocacies

220
00:13:31,352 --> 00:13:33,270
<i>and programs of Angels of Grace.</i>

221
00:13:33,354 --> 00:13:37,191
<i>Unfortunately, I'm in Batangas,</i>
<i>so I can't be with you there.</i>

222
00:13:37,274 --> 00:13:38,567
Come on.

223
00:13:38,651 --> 00:13:40,444
Just think of the free dinner.

224
00:13:40,528 --> 00:13:44,615
By the way, the reservation is
under Mr. Soriano.

225
00:13:44,698 --> 00:13:45,866
I'm counting on you, okay?

226
00:13:45,950 --> 00:13:47,826
[PRECIOUS HESITATES]

227
00:13:47,910 --> 00:13:49,995
Okay. Okay, sure.

228
00:13:50,621 --> 00:13:51,747
[MOUTHS] I'm sorry.

229
00:13:51,830 --> 00:13:52,873
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

230
00:13:52,957 --> 00:13:54,124
[MOUTHS] No worries.

231
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:01,423
- How was it, Auntie?
- [LYDIA] Oh, total success!

232
00:14:01,507 --> 00:14:02,591
- She said yes.
- Okay?

233
00:14:02,675 --> 00:14:04,176
- Yay!
- She's coming here.

234
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:05,386
- Yes.
- Auntie…

235
00:14:05,469 --> 00:14:06,554
[LYDIA] What?

236
00:14:06,637 --> 00:14:10,140
Do you know who Auntie Pres is dating?

237
00:14:10,975 --> 00:14:12,977
Hasn't she told you?

238
00:14:14,061 --> 00:14:16,230
The only person she mentioned was Brandon.

239
00:14:16,313 --> 00:14:19,692
But I just called him, and I don't think
they're still seeing each other.

240
00:14:20,359 --> 00:14:23,445
Ah, so you really have no idea.

241
00:14:23,529 --> 00:14:27,199
It's Sir Eric.
Your aunt is dating Sir Eric.

242
00:14:27,283 --> 00:14:30,244
Eric? As in, the same Sir Eric?

243
00:14:30,327 --> 00:14:33,873
Yes, the canteen supervisor
at Oliver's school.

244
00:14:33,956 --> 00:14:37,293
I actually think he's already
close with Oliver.

245
00:14:37,376 --> 00:14:39,003
- Mm-hmm.
- Mm-hmm.

246
00:14:39,086 --> 00:14:40,921
[MUSIC BUILDING UP]

247
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:44,675
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

248
00:14:47,803 --> 00:14:50,014
- [MUSIC FADES]
- [TRAFFIC NOISE]

249
00:14:50,598 --> 00:14:52,725
[PRECIOUS] Oh, thank you.

250
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:59,064
I don't know, I'd probably be
a bother in your meeting.

251
00:14:59,148 --> 00:15:01,692
- It's okay.
- I'll stay outside and wait.

252
00:15:01,775 --> 00:15:04,570
Come with me inside.
It will only be a short meeting.

253
00:15:04,653 --> 00:15:07,656
Okay. But I'll stay
at another table, okay?

254
00:15:08,616 --> 00:15:10,826
If you want us to have dinner
once your meeting is done,

255
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:12,036
we can have dinner here.

256
00:15:12,119 --> 00:15:15,080
Okay. Anywhere is fine,
as long as I'm with you.

257
00:15:15,164 --> 00:15:18,375
Miss, I have a reservation
with Mr. Soriano.

258
00:15:18,459 --> 00:15:20,210
Yes, ma'am. Please go this way.

259
00:15:20,294 --> 00:15:21,337
Ah, okay.

260
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:24,298
I'll come with you
to make sure you're not alone.

261
00:15:24,381 --> 00:15:25,466
Okay.

262
00:15:31,263 --> 00:15:32,806
[KEYPAD CLACKS]

263
00:15:36,685 --> 00:15:38,938
[KEYPAD CLACKS]

264
00:15:40,105 --> 00:15:45,444
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

265
00:15:45,527 --> 00:15:46,654
[KEYPAD CLACKS]

266
00:15:49,281 --> 00:15:55,371
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

267
00:15:56,455 --> 00:15:58,165
[KEYPAD CLACKS]

268
00:16:03,003 --> 00:16:04,546
[KEYPAD CLACKS]

269
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:24,274
[COUNTDOWN TICKING ON PHONE]

270
00:16:32,741 --> 00:16:33,784
- Cute.
- Mm-hmm.

271
00:16:33,867 --> 00:16:38,247
Why didn't Auntie Pres tell us
that she was dating Sir Eric?

272
00:16:41,166 --> 00:16:45,838
Well, didn't she hide
her thing with Brandon before?

273
00:16:45,921 --> 00:16:48,048
- Mm, yeah.
- You just caught her.

274
00:16:48,132 --> 00:16:50,634
Maybe she's still shy about it.

275
00:16:51,593 --> 00:16:52,594
Okay.

276
00:16:53,262 --> 00:16:56,098
Well, if they really are dating,

277
00:16:57,349 --> 00:16:59,393
I hope we can meet him.

278
00:16:59,476 --> 00:17:01,270
- To see if he's any good.
- Let her be.

279
00:17:01,353 --> 00:17:03,897
She's 41 years old.
She knows what she's doing.

280
00:17:04,481 --> 00:17:06,316
- [JORDAN] Relax.
- Okay.

281
00:17:08,986 --> 00:17:10,612
[WOMAN] Oh! Ms. Precious is here!

282
00:17:10,696 --> 00:17:12,698
- [SQUEALS] Okay, okay. Auntie!
- She's here.

283
00:17:12,781 --> 00:17:14,241
- [LYDIA] Everyone, hide!
- Wait. Dude!

284
00:17:14,324 --> 00:17:16,035
- Wait, wait, wait.
- Hide, everyone. Hurry!

285
00:17:16,618 --> 00:17:18,537
- Everyone, quiet. Okay?
- Hurry up, Jordan!

286
00:17:26,628 --> 00:17:29,590
- Surprise!
- Surprise!

287
00:17:29,673 --> 00:17:30,883
- [PEOPLE CLAPPING]
- [CHUCKLING]

288
00:17:30,966 --> 00:17:32,426
[PRECIOUS] Billy!

289
00:17:32,509 --> 00:17:35,888
[EVERYONE]
♪ <i>Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

290
00:17:35,971 --> 00:17:39,600
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

291
00:17:39,683 --> 00:17:42,436
[PRECIOUS] Billy, you are
behind all this, aren't you?

292
00:17:42,519 --> 00:17:47,524
<i>♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday</i>
<i>Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

293
00:17:49,485 --> 00:17:56,492
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

294
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:13,592
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

295
00:18:29,066 --> 00:18:36,073
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

296
00:18:51,088 --> 00:18:54,007
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

297
00:18:54,091 --> 00:18:56,176
[PRECIOUS GASPS]
Billy! Oh my God!

298
00:18:57,928 --> 00:18:59,012
Are you okay?

299
00:18:59,930 --> 00:19:01,765
You know him, Auntie?

300
00:19:01,849 --> 00:19:03,183
[PRECIOUS] Uh…

301
00:19:03,267 --> 00:19:04,935
Yes. That's Sir Eric.

302
00:19:05,018 --> 00:19:07,479
I was planning to
tell you about him, Billy.

303
00:19:08,814 --> 00:19:10,649
Billy, I can explain.

304
00:19:11,358 --> 00:19:13,068
I didn't plan to hide it from your aunt--

305
00:19:13,152 --> 00:19:15,237
You just won't leave us alone.

306
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:17,447
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

307
00:19:17,531 --> 00:19:19,950
I only asked for one thing.

308
00:19:20,033 --> 00:19:21,034
Billy--

309
00:19:21,118 --> 00:19:22,411
[BILLY] Just leave.

310
00:19:22,494 --> 00:19:24,246
Stay away from my family.

311
00:19:24,329 --> 00:19:26,081
Billy, what's going on?

312
00:19:26,790 --> 00:19:28,750
How could you be so selfish?

313
00:19:29,459 --> 00:19:30,419
Seriously?

314
00:19:31,461 --> 00:19:34,798
You even made a fool of the person
who raised us and cared for us

315
00:19:34,882 --> 00:19:37,009
when that should have been you?!

316
00:19:39,011 --> 00:19:40,888
He's your father, Billy?

317
00:19:42,139 --> 00:19:44,099
I didn't mean to fool anyone.

318
00:19:46,685 --> 00:19:47,519
Precious…

319
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:48,812
Leave.

320
00:19:49,313 --> 00:19:50,522
You're a liar!

321
00:19:51,982 --> 00:19:53,483
- Precious…
- I said leave!

322
00:19:53,567 --> 00:19:55,819
Never show your face here again! Leave!

323
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:56,945
Get out!

324
00:19:57,029 --> 00:19:58,322
Are you okay?

325
00:20:02,826 --> 00:20:09,791
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

326
00:20:26,642 --> 00:20:33,398
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

327
00:20:33,482 --> 00:20:34,691
<i>Pa!</i>

328
00:20:35,275 --> 00:20:36,610
<i>Pa.</i>

329
00:20:46,954 --> 00:20:49,831
[PRECIOUS CRYING]
<i>Billy, I'm sorry.</i>

330
00:20:49,915 --> 00:20:52,960
<i>If I could only choose a father,</i>
<i>I would've done it.</i>

331
00:20:53,043 --> 00:20:55,295
<i>We're tired of waiting</i>
<i>on you, Enrico.</i>

332
00:20:55,379 --> 00:20:56,672
<i>I don't care anymore.</i>

333
00:20:56,755 --> 00:20:57,965
<i>You want to beat me up?</i>

334
00:20:58,048 --> 00:20:59,383
<i>Just kill me!</i>

335
00:20:59,466 --> 00:21:00,884
<i>If you really can't pay</i>
<i>the money back,</i>

336
00:21:00,968 --> 00:21:02,803
<i>I'll get it from your daughter.</i>

337
00:21:02,886 --> 00:21:06,431
[PRECIOUS] <i>What if he</i>
<i>keeps bothering you?</i>

338
00:21:06,515 --> 00:21:09,434
<i>What if he tells Oliver the truth?</i>

339
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:13,230
<i>Oliver, let's talk.</i>

340
00:21:13,313 --> 00:21:18,402
<i>I know that we made a promise</i>
<i>not to lie to each other.</i>

341
00:21:19,111 --> 00:21:23,573
<i>But I broke that promise.</i>

342
00:21:23,657 --> 00:21:25,450
<i>What do you mean?</i>

343
00:21:29,204 --> 00:21:33,625
<i>You know Sir Eric,</i>
<i>the guy you met at school?</i>
